			"notes": "Initial public release — v1.1.0\nMCServerHost is a universal Minecraft plugin/mod that restores true player IP addresses for servers running behind MCServerHost's proxy infrastructure. When players connect through the proxy, their real IP is embedded in the handshake payload — this plugin intercepts that payload, validates it, and rewrites the connection so the backend server sees the player's actual IP and hostname rather than the proxy's.\n\nSupported platforms: Bukkit/Spigot/Paper, BungeeCord, Velocity, and Forge (1.16.5 – 1.21.x)\n\nKey features:\n\nHandshake-level IP and hostname rewriting across all supported platforms\nGeyser/Floodgate support for Bedrock players via session secrets\nPlayer transfer to a hub server on shutdown, using either the modern Player.transfer() API or legacy BungeeCord plugin messaging\nProtocolLib integration (optional, preferred when available)\nMixin-based bytecode injection for Forge compatibility across major version ranges\nJava 8 compatible through Forge 1.16.5; supports Java 8–25 on modern versions"
		}
